            <ArticleTitle>Tubal sterilisation without consent: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>114-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Tubal sterilisation is practised all over the world. This safe, easy and highly effective, long-term method for birth control can be carried out during the hospital stay for either a normal delivery or caesarean section. In India, female sterilisation accounts for 37.3% of all methods of family planning.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
